From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qasf: Don't restart the reader when seeking a stopped filter.

The filter graph seeks every source after stopping its filters
(MediaFilter_Stop() sets the current position again). The ASF reader's
ChangeCurrent() then stopped and restarted the WM async reader although
the filter was stopped: the reader streamed again, delivering samples
and end of stream to the stopped renderers, and the next seek waited
for its WMT_STOPPED status from a callback thread which could be blocked
in a renderer.

A stopped filter has nothing to restart: keep the new position for the
next run, as native does.

Game impacted: Border Break Scramble (Sega RingEdge 2): its movie
teardown stops the graph while its video renderer forwards the seek
upstream holding its own lock, the lock its EndOfStream() waits for on
the reader's callback thread: a deadlock after the first attract movie,
the attract screen then blank (and the window thread blocked) for good.
---
--- a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
@@ -404,6 +404,12 @@
 
     TRACE("iface %p.\n", iface);
 
+    /* A stopped filter has no streaming to restart: the new position is used
+     * when the graph runs. Restarting the reader here would deliver samples
+     * to stopped renderers (the graph seeks every source when it stops). */
+    if (filter->filter.state == State_Stopped)
+        return S_OK;
+
     /* Send begin flush commands downstream. */
     for (i = 0; i < filter->stream_count; ++i)
     {
